==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|goh|argerōn}}, from {{inh|de|gmh|argern||worsen}}. Derived from {{der|de|goh|arg|t=bad}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*argaz}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʔɛɐ̯ɡɐn/}}
* {{audio|de|De-ärgern.ogg|audio}}
* {{rhymes|de|ɛʁn}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-weak|ärgert|ärgerte|geärgert}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[annoy]], to [[make]] [[angry]] (''+accusative'')
#: {{ux|de|Die anderen Kinder '''ärgern''' ihn immer.|The other kids keep '''annoying''' him.}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[be]] [[annoyed]], to [[be]] [[angry]], to [[get]] [[annoyed]], to [[get]] [[angry]]

